{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And you shall place the parochet, etc., and you shall bring there.</b> From here it appears that he is to hang the parochet in its place first, and afterward bring the ark inside the parochet. But in parashat Pekudei (Exodus 40:3) HaShem said to him: ״וְשַׂמְתָּ שָׁם אֶת אֲרוֹן הָעֵדוּת וְסַכֹּתָ עַל הָאָרוֹן אֶת הַפָּרֹכֶת״ — which implies that he is to set the ark first. And so Moses did, for he set the ark first, as is explained there (Exodus 40:20)." "And it appears that the reason he placed the setting of the parochet before the bringing of the ark is only that he wished to complete the making of the parochet; but as for the order of which one precedes, that is stated in parashat Pekudei. Or it may be because the order of the erection does not belong here but in parashat Pekudei, and the bringing of the ark was mentioned here only to explain what the parochet serves for and what its function is — namely, to divide between the Kodesh and Kodesh HaKodashim, which is the place of the ark. Therefore he did not specify which comes first. We shall investigate this in its place."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:42.177808932Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}